{"uid":"db163588dd86ac02","name":"test_clicking_from_the_list_into_a_run_and_back_leaves_one_refresh_loop","fullName":"tests.test_browser_hub_refresh_loop_clicks#test_clicking_from_the_list_into_a_run_and_back_leaves_one_refresh_loop","historyId":"475380e884e9740886eb45d62cec465f","time":{"start":1791963446706,"stop":1791963460433,"duration":13727},"description":"Click the run-list's own `<a href=\"#/run/...\">` link into the detail\n    view, then -- before its detail fetch resolves -- click the detail\n    view's own `<a href=\"#/\">` (\"&larr; runs\") link back to the list. This\n    targets the exact guard task 016 added at the end of `renderRunDetail`\n    (`if (myGen === renderGeneration) refreshTimer = startRefreshLoop(load);`):\n    without it, the detail render's `load()` -- still in flight when the\n    click back to the list fires -- unconditionally installs its own timer\n    once its delayed fetch finally resolves, on top of the one the list view\n    (correctly) installed for itself, orphaning it. Reverting just that one\n    `if` guard (matching task 016's own revert-evidence pattern) makes this\n    test observe `2` live loops instead of `1`.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Click the run-list's own <code>&lt;a href=&quot;#/run/...&quot;&gt;</code> link into the detail<br />\nview, then -- before its detail fetch resolves -- click the detail<br />\nview's own <code>&lt;a href=&quot;#/&quot;&gt;</code> (&quot;← runs&quot;) link back to the list. This<br />\ntargets the exact guard task 016 added at the end of <code>renderRunDetail</code><br />\n(<code>if (myGen === renderGeneration) refreshTimer = startRefreshLoop(load);</code>):<br />\nwithout it, the detail render's <code>load()</code> -- still in flight when the<br />\nclick back to the list fires -- unconditionally installs its own timer<br />\nonce its delayed fetch finally resolves, on top of the one the list view<br />\n(correctly) installed for itself, orphaning it. Reverting just that one<br />\n